<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/3rd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Raphia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/217-bce">217 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-syrian-war">Fourth Syrian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Raphia was fought in 217 BCE near Gaza during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-syrian-war">Fourth Syrian War</a>, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-iv-philopator">Ptolemy IV</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and the Seleucid king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antiochus-iii-the-great">Antiochus III</a>. The Ptolemaic army won, with native Egyptian troops playing a significant role. The battle encouraged the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemaic-kingdom">Ptolemaic Empire</a> to recruit more <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egyptians">Egyptians</a> into its army, which in turn altered the balance of power within society.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-raphia.jpg" alt="Battle of Raphia" width="320" height="235" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Javierfv1212 (talk) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_raphia.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
